      "writtenOn": "2026-05-07T17:20:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "nit: it seems a bit cleaner to read the host\u0027s value into a temporary variable first, and then assign it to `kvm-\u003earch.apic_bus_cycle_ns` only if it is non-zero (so that we don\u0027t need to \"re-initialize\" it back to APIC_BUS_CYCLE_NS_DEFAULT)?\n\nBTW actually it seems it would be nice to move this whole \"postponed per-VM setup\" (i.e. the setup which is not really about the vCPU) out of `__vcpu_create()` to a separate function called from here in `__vcpu_create()` (was there any reason why we didn\u0027t do that from the beginning?). So that, in particular, that temporary apic_bus_cycle_ns variable would be a local variable of that function, and thus wouldn\u0027t \"pollute\" the local variables of `__vcpu_create()`.",
      "revId": "d9a8e6be9b1b7167c4422e129aef05ab4e7d6a63",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
